                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Epidemiology is a core course for undergraduate students majoring in preventive medicine. The course consists of 54 contact hours (2-4 hours per week over 16 weeks) and carries 3 credits. Delivered in Chinese, it employs lectures and in-class quizzes to enable students to master core epidemiological concepts, fundamental principles of research design, and problem-solving skills using epidemiological approaches. Prerequisites: Health Statistics. Co-requisite: Epidemiology Practice.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
